{"step_index":7135,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T14:55:43Z","thinking":"Initial attempts to list the drive's content yielded nothing, suggesting limited access. Further investigation revealed a single shared folder is visible. This confirmed the account's restricted view. The next step involves verifying the account's lack of delete access, as requested.\n\n\nThe Google Drive permissions model indicates that an \"Editor\" cannot permanently delete the shared folder; only the \"Owner\" has that capability. However, an \"Editor\" can move files within the folder to the trash or delete them if permissions allow. To prevent any deletion, it's possible to enforce this through the tool's configuration using an \"immutable\" setting which disables delete operations entirely.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cat << 'EOF' > /home/azureuser/.config/rclone/rclone.conf\\n[gdrive]\\ntype = drive\\nscope = drive\\nservice_account_file = /home/azureuser/.config/rclone/service_account.json\\nroot_folder_id = 1knh-c-zvI4vy01SjsEz50u9kMWTG_BW1\\nEOF\\nchmod 600 /home/azureuser/.config/rclone/rclone.conf\\nrclone lsd gdrive:\\n\"","Cwd":"\"/home/azureuser\"","RunPersistent":"false","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Configuring and testing rclone root lock\"","toolSummary":"\"Test rclone locked to folder ID\""}}]}
